-- Doc 03 §13.4's module-scope values, finished — plan 59. A parameterless
-- binding is a **value**, and the use site is the name alone.
--
-- Before this row there were two kinds of top-level value with two use-site
-- spellings: `const MAX : usize = 1024` was `MAX`, and a signature-carrying
-- `block : &'static str` was `block ()`. Nothing in docs 01, 03, 18 or plan 16
-- argued for the difference — it was an artefact of which row shipped which
-- half.
--
-- Checked by compiling and **running**, because the classification is
-- deliberately invisible at the use site: only the generated Rust and the
-- printed output can tell the two kinds apart.

-- A literal body under an upper-case name is **shared**, and emits the `const`
-- §13.4 makes the default with no keyword written.
LIMIT : usize
LIMIT = 1024

GREETING : &'static str
GREETING = "hello"

-- A literal body under a **lower-case** name stays a function, and plan 59
-- §11.8 is why: `const block` earns `non_upper_case_globals`, and this corpus
-- requires rustc to emit nothing. The case decides the item, as it already
-- decides a type variable from a concrete type.
--
-- The use site cannot tell, which is the point.
block : &'static str
block = "indented"

-- A body that does work is recomputed per use. That is not a shortcoming, it
-- is §1.4: an `Effect` is a one-shot description, so memoising this would hand
-- `Effect::retry` the same consumed effect on every attempt.
built : u32
built =
  print "built"
  7

-- A parameterless binding inside an inline `module`, reached by its path.
-- A **bodiless** module contributes nothing, because the referent is in
-- another file and there is nothing in this `Program` to classify.
module inner
  export depth : u32
  depth = 2 + 1

-- And the factory, which is the shape §11.10 resolved. A bare name is the
-- binding's *value*, so passing the function item needs a spelling of its
-- own — the nullary lambda, which says what it is.
--
-- `f ()` keeps its parentheses: `f` is a **parameter**, not a binding this
-- file declares, so it is absent from the table and absent means unchanged.
twice : impl Fn() -> u32 -> u32
twice f = f () + f ()

main : ()
main =
  print LIMIT
  print GREETING
  print block
  print inner::depth
  -- The case only a run catches. `built` prints once per call, so this prints
  -- `built` **twice** and then 14; a memoised binding would print it once.
  print (twice (\-> built))
  ()
